<title>KENYA: Kenyan cocktail kills 20.</title>
<headline>Kenyan cocktail kills 20.</headline>
<dateline>NAIROBI 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Some 20 people have died in central Kenya in the last two days after drinking a cocktail of an illegal traditional brew laced with contaminated alcohol, Nairobi newspapers reported on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The Daily Nation newspaper said the deaths occurred in the coffee and tea growing district of Murang'a, around 100 km (60 miles) from the capital Nairobi.</p>
<p>The illegal brew known as &quot;chang'aa&quot; is a favourite of rural folk too poor to afford beer. Police are investigating the deaths.</p>
